title: 'pallet-whitelist: permissionless authorized dispatch'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `dispatch_whitelisted_call` and `dispatch_whitelisted_call_with_preimage` gain
    `#[pallet::authorize]` callbacks: an unsigned submission is admitted at the transaction
    pool if `DispatchWhitelistedOrigin::try_origin(Authorized)` passes and the call hash is in
    `WhitelistedCall`. `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` converts the `None` origin into `Authorized`
    for the dispatch body. Dispatch bodies are unchanged and no new `Config` item is added.

    Adds `frame_system::EnsureAuthorized`. A runtime opts in by including it in
    `DispatchWhitelistedOrigin`, e.g. `EitherOf<EnsureRoot<AccountId>, EnsureAuthorized<AccountId>>`;
    leaving it out keeps the current behavior.

crates:
- name: pallet-whitelist
  bump: minor
- name: frame-system
  bump: minor
